1
00:00:14,740 --> 00:00:18,270
♪I stretch and yawn
when the sun is high in the sky♪

2
00:00:19,170 --> 00:00:23,030
♪A cup of tea and a little tune,
what a carefree life♪

3
00:00:23,890 --> 00:00:28,480
♪The fortune teller said
love would come my way this year♪

4
00:00:28,740 --> 00:00:32,580
♪But all I see is my food
arriving right on time♪

5
00:00:33,850 --> 00:00:35,670
♪No rush, no worries♪

6
00:00:35,670 --> 00:00:38,360
♪Love is all a matter of chance♪

7
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:40,480
♪Flowers bloom and fade♪

8
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:43,380
♪I'd rather take good care
of myself first♪

9
00:00:43,380 --> 00:00:45,580
♪Two orioles sing among
the green willows♪

10
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:47,970
♪And I still don't have a boyfriend♪

11
00:00:48,180 --> 00:00:50,590
♪My best years are nothing
to worry about♪

12
00:00:50,590 --> 00:00:53,240
♪I'll stay happily single
till I'm old and gray♪

13
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:07,540
=Besties' Coming Fortune=

14
00:01:07,580 --> 00:01:09,740
=Episode 3=

15
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:11,390
My Lady.

16
00:01:11,840 --> 00:01:12,430
Third Madam.

17
00:01:12,870 --> 00:01:14,070
The Heir's poison suddenly flared up

18
00:01:14,070 --> 00:01:14,840
on his way back to the manor.

19
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:16,000
His carriage is outside right now.

20
00:01:16,230 --> 00:01:17,030
Please help him.

21
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:19,230
Here, take this.

22
00:01:19,230 --> 00:01:19,870
Hold this for me.

23
00:01:20,230 --> 00:01:21,000
See you inside in a bit.

24
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:21,510
Wait.

25
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:22,590
Eat more.

26
00:01:24,480 --> 00:01:25,030
Over here.

27
00:01:38,230 --> 00:01:38,980
Shen Cheng.

28
00:01:41,510 --> 00:01:42,390
Shen Cheng,

29
00:01:43,430 --> 00:01:44,200
hang in there.

30
00:01:44,310 --> 00:01:45,320
Let me help you up.

31
00:02:03,220 --> 00:02:04,880
Look, First Madam!

32
00:02:05,510 --> 00:02:07,280
The Heir's wife is so impatient

33
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:08,480
to get it on with her lover.

34
00:02:08,630 --> 00:02:09,950
They're already at it in the carriage...

35
00:02:12,430 --> 00:02:13,840
As the Heir's wife,

36
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:15,160
how dare she engage
in such shameful acts

37
00:02:15,310 --> 00:02:17,320
in front of everyone?

38
00:02:17,960 --> 00:02:19,320
Go pull back the curtain.

39
00:02:19,920 --> 00:02:20,990
I want to see for myself.

40
00:02:22,120 --> 00:02:22,800
I know you don't want

41
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:23,560
anyone to find out.

42
00:02:23,960 --> 00:02:24,670
I'll help you.

43
00:02:41,270 --> 00:02:41,870
Come on.

44
00:02:41,870 --> 00:02:42,480
Hurry.

45
00:02:45,910 --> 00:02:46,480
Quick.

46
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:50,780
Get lost.

47
00:02:50,780 --> 00:02:51,380
(Shen Manor)

48
00:02:51,870 --> 00:02:52,240
Bestie,

49
00:02:52,240 --> 00:02:52,760
I'm here.

50
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:53,830
Keep them busy for me.

51
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:54,440
Alright.

52
00:02:55,280 --> 00:02:56,890
What perfect timing, Shutiao.

53
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:57,600
What?

54
00:02:57,910 --> 00:02:59,550
So you knew
there was a scandal unfolding inside,

55
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:01,670
and that's why
you came to cover for Yuyuan?

56
00:03:01,870 --> 00:03:02,870
Mind your own business.

57
00:03:02,870 --> 00:03:03,360
Come

58
00:03:03,750 --> 00:03:05,440
hold Third Madam down.

59
00:03:07,630 --> 00:03:08,440
Let me go.

60
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:10,630
Do you know who's inside?

61
00:03:10,630 --> 00:03:11,550
You can't scare me.

62
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:12,950
Don't tell me it's the Heir.

63
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:14,320
Xiangchun,

64
00:03:15,150 --> 00:03:15,950
get your weapons.

65
00:03:16,080 --> 00:03:18,160
Let's teach those lovebirds a lesson.

66
00:03:25,310 --> 00:03:26,990
Forgive us, My Lady.

67
00:03:54,680 --> 00:03:55,440
How dare you.

68
00:03:56,990 --> 00:03:58,230
Let's see who dares touch her.

69
00:03:58,360 --> 00:03:58,950
Your...

70
00:03:59,250 --> 00:04:00,480
Your Lordship.

71
00:04:05,080 --> 00:04:05,480
Come on.

72
00:04:11,840 --> 00:04:12,760
Old Madam,

73
00:04:13,430 --> 00:04:14,710
(Old Madam of the Marquis's Manor)
I was only trying

74
00:04:14,710 --> 00:04:16,830
to protect
the Marquis's family's reputation.

75
00:04:17,070 --> 00:04:18,800
In my haste,

76
00:04:19,070 --> 00:04:21,320
I offended the Heir's wife.

77
00:04:24,270 --> 00:04:25,880
Anyone can put on an act.

78
00:04:26,270 --> 00:04:26,640
Bestie,

79
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:27,830
give her a taste of her own medicine.

80
00:04:37,430 --> 00:04:41,030
Oh, heavens.

81
00:04:46,270 --> 00:04:47,800
The Heir and I were merely

82
00:04:47,800 --> 00:04:49,560
enjoying some intimacy
as husband and wife.

83
00:04:50,120 --> 00:04:51,590
Yet you slander us like this.

84
00:04:52,510 --> 00:04:53,880
What's the point

85
00:04:54,070 --> 00:04:54,800
of being the Heir's wife

86
00:04:55,630 --> 00:04:57,270
if this is how I'm treated?

87
00:04:57,680 --> 00:04:59,440
I don't want to live anymore.

88
00:05:02,630 --> 00:05:05,030
Life in this manor is unbearable.

89
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:07,000
Even the Wife of the Marquis's Heir

90
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:08,470
gets bullied like this.

91
00:05:08,750 --> 00:05:10,760
I don't want to live either.

92
00:05:19,430 --> 00:05:20,350
How dare you!

93
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:22,070
You spread baseless rumors

94
00:05:22,070 --> 00:05:22,950
and falsely accused your mistress.

95
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:24,150
Won't you admit your guilt?

96
00:05:24,510 --> 00:05:25,830
Have mercy, Old Madam.

97
00:05:26,070 --> 00:05:26,430
I...

98
00:05:26,430 --> 00:05:28,200
I simply wasn't thinking straight.

99
00:05:28,430 --> 00:05:29,720
Have mercy, Old Madam.

100
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:31,270
Please spare me, Old Madam.

101
00:05:31,270 --> 00:05:33,040
I know I was wrong.

102
00:05:33,040 --> 00:05:34,640
- Have mercy, Old Madam.
- You dared defy your superiors.

103
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:36,910
You think admitting
your mistake is enough?

104
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:39,510
Then

105
00:05:40,070 --> 00:05:41,120
give her fifty strokes

106
00:05:41,120 --> 00:05:41,950
and throw her out of the manor.

107
00:05:43,360 --> 00:05:43,830
Cheng,

108
00:05:44,360 --> 00:05:45,830
Xiangchun is a pitiful woman.

109
00:05:46,120 --> 00:05:47,510
She has no one to rely on here.

110
00:05:47,510 --> 00:05:48,680
Could we perhaps

111
00:05:48,680 --> 00:05:49,470
spare her the beating?

112
00:05:50,160 --> 00:05:51,640
If Xiangchun had no one backing her,

113
00:05:51,930 --> 00:05:53,150
would she dare stir up trouble?

114
00:05:53,580 --> 00:05:56,150
Could someone be pulling the strings?

115
00:05:56,620 --> 00:05:57,880
I wonder who it could be.

116
00:06:00,830 --> 00:06:02,150
Why are you looking at me?

117
00:06:03,270 --> 00:06:04,350
It wasn't me.

118
00:06:04,830 --> 00:06:06,510
Don't just say it.

119
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:08,560
Swear it.

120
00:06:09,510 --> 00:06:11,830
If you were the one behind this, Xiang,

121
00:06:12,480 --> 00:06:13,830
may you trip whenever you walk,

122
00:06:13,830 --> 00:06:14,870
get bitten by dogs when you go out,

123
00:06:14,870 --> 00:06:15,680
have your silver stolen,

124
00:06:15,680 --> 00:06:16,830
and lose your hair.

125
00:06:17,680 --> 00:06:18,910
Go on, say it.

126
00:06:19,870 --> 00:06:21,000
We're all family.

127
00:06:21,830 --> 00:06:23,710
There's no need
for such frightening words.

128
00:06:25,510 --> 00:06:26,080
Alright,

129
00:06:26,430 --> 00:06:27,640
I failed to discipline her properly.

130
00:06:28,270 --> 00:06:28,950
This time,

131
00:06:29,190 --> 00:06:30,910
Yuyuan was nearly falsely accused.

132
00:06:31,070 --> 00:06:32,750
I suppose I'm to blame as well.

133
00:06:32,750 --> 00:06:33,640
- Good.
- I...

134
00:06:37,270 --> 00:06:38,880
Since Xiang has admitted her mistake,

135
00:06:39,360 --> 00:06:39,910
Grandmother,

136
00:06:40,270 --> 00:06:41,270
you can decide her punishment.

137
00:06:41,270 --> 00:06:41,910
No, wait.

138
00:06:42,160 --> 00:06:42,430
I...

139
00:06:42,430 --> 00:06:42,910
Alright.

140
00:06:43,120 --> 00:06:44,430
Since you can't manage
the household properly,

141
00:06:44,430 --> 00:06:46,120
you needn't manage it anymore.

142
00:06:46,480 --> 00:06:47,750
Hand over the household management

143
00:06:47,750 --> 00:06:48,510
token.

144
00:06:52,460 --> 00:06:54,900
(Shen)

145
00:07:00,830 --> 00:07:01,560
Grandmother,

146
00:07:01,920 --> 00:07:03,360
Xiang is glaring at us.

147
00:07:03,360 --> 00:07:03,760
I...

148
00:07:04,070 --> 00:07:05,510
I just feel sorry for them.

149
00:07:06,070 --> 00:07:07,510
If you feel sorry for them,

150
00:07:08,240 --> 00:07:09,510
why not show it?

151
00:07:15,070 --> 00:07:15,680
Consider

152
00:07:16,560 --> 00:07:18,470
this my apology to you both.

153
00:07:21,630 --> 00:07:23,120
This bracelet doesn't look valuable.

154
00:07:23,120 --> 00:07:24,470
Didn't you study artifact restoration?

155
00:07:24,680 --> 00:07:26,000
Put your expertise to work.

156
00:07:26,430 --> 00:07:26,800
Go on.

157
00:07:31,830 --> 00:07:33,070
But this

158
00:07:33,070 --> 00:07:34,470
is your personal jewelry, Xiang.

159
00:07:34,680 --> 00:07:35,880
It's far too precious.

160
00:07:36,630 --> 00:07:37,680
We'll just

161
00:07:37,680 --> 00:07:39,000
pick a couple of other things.

162
00:07:39,590 --> 00:07:41,910
I remember your dowry

163
00:07:42,240 --> 00:07:43,760
included something called

164
00:07:43,830 --> 00:07:46,940
a gold phoenix hairpin
with kesi silk and inlaid gems.

165
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:47,560
(Wretches!)

166
00:07:47,680 --> 00:07:48,830
(They always pick
the most expensive things.)

167
00:07:48,830 --> 00:07:52,390
And a set of solid gold
hair ornaments with red coral, right?

168
00:07:52,750 --> 00:07:55,030
Which one do you want?

169
00:07:55,030 --> 00:07:56,800
Only children have to choose.

170
00:07:57,310 --> 00:07:58,680
We'll take both.

171
00:07:59,870 --> 00:08:01,350
- Thank you, Xiang.
- Thank you, Xiang.

172
00:08:03,630 --> 00:08:04,120
Xiangchun,

173
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:04,910
let's go.

174
00:08:15,720 --> 00:08:16,240
Old Madam.

175
00:08:17,270 --> 00:08:17,910
Cheng,

176
00:08:18,430 --> 00:08:20,200
tomorrow is your parents'
death anniversary.

177
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:22,680
Everyone in the manor
is observing mourning rites.

178
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:24,350
Grandmother,

179
00:08:24,680 --> 00:08:25,640
I have urgent matters to attend to.

180
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:26,510
I'll take my leave.

181
00:08:34,480 --> 00:08:35,110
My Lady,

182
00:08:35,240 --> 00:08:35,800
Third Madam,

183
00:08:36,030 --> 00:08:37,110
these are for you both.

184
00:08:42,660 --> 00:08:44,780
(Fortune)

185
00:08:44,840 --> 00:08:46,520
Old Madam, please don't worry too much.

186
00:08:46,910 --> 00:08:48,110
The Heir is like this every year.

187
00:08:48,110 --> 00:08:49,440
His parents died under
suspicious circumstances

188
00:08:49,910 --> 00:08:51,710
during the Battle of Qiyun Pass.

189
00:08:52,080 --> 00:08:53,710
He's never been able
to come to terms with it.

190
00:08:54,120 --> 00:08:55,440
He avoids the memorial rites

191
00:08:55,440 --> 00:08:57,160
simply because he refuses to accept

192
00:08:57,480 --> 00:08:59,920
that they're already gone.

193
00:09:00,270 --> 00:09:01,830
Judging by how affectionate

194
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:04,230
the Heir and his wife were
in the carriage last night,

195
00:09:04,630 --> 00:09:05,400
perhaps

196
00:09:05,510 --> 00:09:06,320
we could ask the Heir's wife

197
00:09:06,320 --> 00:09:07,800
to talk some sense into him.

198
00:09:13,480 --> 00:09:14,350
Me?

199
00:09:17,270 --> 00:09:18,360
Me?

200
00:09:38,360 --> 00:09:39,590
Who told you to do all this?

201
00:09:41,750 --> 00:09:42,440
Wait a minute.

202
00:09:44,750 --> 00:09:45,350
What?

203
00:09:45,840 --> 00:09:47,470
Are you going to be like Grandmother

204
00:09:48,630 --> 00:09:50,270
and tell me to stop avoiding the past?

205
00:09:50,270 --> 00:09:51,400
Who said I was going to lecture you?

206
00:09:52,440 --> 00:09:53,350
What's wrong with avoiding things?

207
00:09:54,480 --> 00:09:55,840
Avoidance is a natural human instinct,

208
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:56,640
isn't it?

209
00:09:57,320 --> 00:09:58,710
Instead of pushing yourself so hard,

210
00:09:58,960 --> 00:10:00,490
why not give yourself a break?

211
00:10:00,680 --> 00:10:01,520
Do you really believe that?

212
00:10:01,720 --> 00:10:02,370
Of course.

213
00:10:02,940 --> 00:10:04,400
Actually, where I come from,

214
00:10:04,600 --> 00:10:05,970
we also have a custom
of hanging red silk ribbons.

215
00:10:06,360 --> 00:10:07,610
People say

216
00:10:07,960 --> 00:10:09,480
that once the ribbons are hung,

217
00:10:10,660 --> 00:10:11,800
our departed loved ones

218
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:13,660
(Health)
can hear how much we miss them.

219
00:10:14,030 --> 00:10:15,590
After my grandmother passed away,

220
00:10:16,840 --> 00:10:18,040
I never dared to hang one.

221
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:20,350
It felt as though

222
00:10:20,750 --> 00:10:22,230
doing so would mean she was really gone.

223
00:10:23,270 --> 00:10:24,920
Then one day, I dreamed of her.

224
00:10:26,840 --> 00:10:28,460
She told me in my dream

225
00:10:29,550 --> 00:10:30,630
that she was up in heaven,

226
00:10:30,630 --> 00:10:31,750
waiting for me all along,

227
00:10:32,480 --> 00:10:33,800
hoping to hear my voice.

228
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:36,110
From that day on,

229
00:10:36,630 --> 00:10:37,950
I started hanging one every year.

230
00:10:39,870 --> 00:10:41,160
I'm not trying to persuade you.

231
00:10:41,870 --> 00:10:43,080
If you don't want to do it,

232
00:10:43,080 --> 00:10:44,440
I can do it for you.

233
00:10:45,240 --> 00:10:46,200
I just don't want you

234
00:10:46,200 --> 00:10:47,040
to end up like me,

235
00:10:47,630 --> 00:10:48,590
living with regrets.

236
00:10:51,900 --> 00:10:58,420
♪Let the gentle breeze begin
the story of our love♪

237
00:10:58,990 --> 00:11:02,410
♪Watch as the bright moon slowly♪

238
00:11:05,510 --> 00:11:06,160
Look.

239
00:11:07,630 --> 00:11:09,240
They really heard us!

240
00:11:09,720 --> 00:11:10,990
They heard us.

241
00:11:12,890 --> 00:11:16,430
♪You are the most beautiful encounter♪

242
00:11:17,040 --> 00:11:20,050
♪In all my years
of wandering through lifetimes♪

243
00:11:20,240 --> 00:11:23,660
♪Hand in hand, we'll walk through♪

244
00:11:25,440 --> 00:11:29,690
♪Spring, summer, fall, and winter♪

245
00:11:30,080 --> 00:11:30,860
Girl,

246
00:11:31,220 --> 00:11:32,420
I'm totally shipping you.

247
00:11:34,600 --> 00:11:35,560
Starting today,

248
00:11:36,210 --> 00:11:36,990
I hereby declare myself

249
00:11:37,630 --> 00:11:39,550
the number one fan of

250
00:11:39,550 --> 00:11:40,800
the Yuyuan and Cheng couple.

251
00:11:40,910 --> 00:11:41,590
Stop right there.

252
00:11:41,900 --> 00:11:43,310
Don't go shipping us.

253
00:11:43,630 --> 00:11:45,520
Other couples shower each other
with affection.

254
00:11:45,870 --> 00:11:47,560
Have you ever seen one
shower each other with blood?

255
00:11:50,750 --> 00:11:52,200
You've got it better.

256
00:11:53,080 --> 00:11:54,630
At least Shen He

257
00:11:54,630 --> 00:11:56,230
seems like a normal person.

258
00:11:58,030 --> 00:11:59,110
Normal?

259
00:11:59,480 --> 00:12:00,920
He's into some pretty wild stuff.

260
00:12:06,750 --> 00:12:07,630
Everything that happens

261
00:12:07,630 --> 00:12:09,160
between her and me from now on,

262
00:12:10,790 --> 00:12:12,710
you must record word for word.

263
00:12:22,360 --> 00:12:23,280
The deceased

264
00:12:23,790 --> 00:12:24,160
is female.

265
00:12:25,480 --> 00:12:25,990
Height,

266
00:12:26,550 --> 00:12:28,280
four chi and eight cun.

267
00:12:30,080 --> 00:12:30,630
Pardon me.

268
00:12:32,840 --> 00:12:35,470
There's a crescent-shaped tattoo
on her arm.

269
00:12:39,270 --> 00:12:40,110
Just above her neck,

270
00:12:40,510 --> 00:12:41,920
a long nail has been driven in.

271
00:12:44,790 --> 00:12:46,160
This specially made type of nail

272
00:12:46,630 --> 00:12:47,630
is only available in military camps

273
00:12:48,290 --> 00:12:49,920
and the Imperial Guards.

274
00:12:50,510 --> 00:12:51,710
Whoever killed her

275
00:12:52,440 --> 00:12:53,110
is no ordinary person.

276
00:12:53,270 --> 00:12:53,920
Young Master,

277
00:12:54,550 --> 00:12:56,160
your stand-in at the brothel
can't hold out much longer.

278
00:12:56,630 --> 00:12:57,830
If the Heir finds out

279
00:12:58,120 --> 00:12:58,840
that I told you

280
00:12:58,840 --> 00:13:00,270
the body connected
to General Qin was here

281
00:13:00,270 --> 00:13:01,320
and brought you here to examine it,

282
00:13:01,320 --> 00:13:02,870
he'll beat me to death.

283
00:13:02,870 --> 00:13:03,590
What are you afraid of?

284
00:13:04,390 --> 00:13:05,950
My brother can't control me anymore.

285
00:13:08,630 --> 00:13:09,790
Just look at all

286
00:13:09,790 --> 00:13:11,230
the trouble we're caught up in.

287
00:13:12,480 --> 00:13:13,040
Girl,

288
00:13:13,550 --> 00:13:14,480
do you think we'll survive

289
00:13:14,480 --> 00:13:15,560
until the original heroines return?

290
00:13:17,250 --> 00:13:18,310
Of course we will.

291
00:13:19,080 --> 00:13:20,350
Instead of waiting to be attacked,

292
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:21,560
we should strike first.

293
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:23,920
Tell me more.

294
00:13:24,190 --> 00:13:26,710
From my years of reading novels,

295
00:13:27,080 --> 00:13:29,160
household scheming always follows
the same tricks.

296
00:13:30,550 --> 00:13:33,080
We just need to counter them

297
00:13:33,080 --> 00:13:34,760
one by one to stay out of danger.

298
00:13:35,240 --> 00:13:36,310
First,

299
00:13:36,460 --> 00:13:37,830
the most notorious trick

300
00:13:39,270 --> 00:13:40,160
is

301
00:13:40,370 --> 00:13:42,010
the poisoning scheme.

302
00:13:48,800 --> 00:13:51,120
♪No matter how
the universe changes tomorrow♪

303
00:13:51,120 --> 00:13:58,320
♪Right now,
I just want to stay by your side♪

304
00:13:58,320 --> 00:14:03,520
♪Let this kiss and this dream
last until we're old♪

305
00:14:04,740 --> 00:14:09,760
♪And hold on to all
the tenderness of this moment♪

306
00:14:11,140 --> 00:14:16,220
♪Following this heartbeat,
we'll retrace our steps♪

307
00:14:17,560 --> 00:14:22,680
♪As time goes by,
all I need is your gaze♪

308
00:14:23,960 --> 00:14:27,350
♪One dream until our hair turns gray♪

309
00:14:46,080 --> 00:14:49,450
♪One dream until our hair turns gray♪
